From bce722f6798cf49765a9bcc2c07a5f25dad47ed6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:54:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Importer: deep-link cross-regulation citations to the
 cited provision

Cross-regulation citations ("Regulation Number 7, Part B, Section I.B.33")
now link to /regulations/{key}#{provision id} instead of the top of the
other regulation. A committed id index (pipeline/out/corpus_ids.json,
built by the new `dump-ids` subcommand and verified against production)
lets resolve_cross_reg_target pick the exact provision, else the nearest
existing ancestor, else the part root, else the regulation root (no link).

- link_citations steps 2/2b/1.6: one link per cited section; the trailing
  "and Section II.B." after a cross-regulation cite never binds to the
  current document's own id any more (21 such same-document links removed)
- General Permit condition references resolve the same way
- Common Provisions section links gain the #sec-cp-... hash
- unresolved_cross_reg bucket in the diff report (source id + citation)
- empty/absent index: output byte-for-byte unchanged (tested)
- import.yml: dump-ids runs before parse
- link_change_report.py + out/sprint2_link_changes.md: before/after report

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WUMyyKmSdfgERmWRQHrjdT
