From 4dbd26a24aca49496711624c242e876804ac9a6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:55:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Exact official-source links for AQCC regulations and ECMC
 2 CCR 404-1

REG_META source_url for the 31 AQCC documents and ECMC now points at the
Colorado Secretary of State's stable per-rule page
(DisplayRule.do?action=ruleinfo&ruleId=...), which always shows the current
version, instead of the generic cdphe.colorado.gov/aqcc-regulations and
ecmc.colorado.gov/regulatory/rules index pages. Each URL was fetched on
2026-10-03 and its page heading matched the CCR number and title; the ruleIds
are the ones already recorded in pipeline/sources/manifest.json.

Tests that asserted the old generic URL now assert the exact one, and a new
ExactSosSourceUrlTests class pins every value against the manifest.

Adds supabase/migrations/RUN_ME_20261003_exact_source_urls.sql (NOT applied):
updates provisions.source_url by reg_key for rows still on the old generic URL
(19,132 rows read from production: every provision of these regulations carries
the URL, not just the root).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WUMyyKmSdfgERmWRQHrjdT
