From 760f659e9be5ce89692d89d1b9d5622b691245b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:00:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Reader navigation sprint 2: jump-box keyboard,
 cross-regulation preview, return link
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Jump box is an ARIA combobox/listbox: ArrowDown/ArrowUp move the active
  option (wrapping), Enter opens it (or the first result, or an exact
  provision id / citation when nothing is listed), Escape closes the list.
- A plain click on a hashed .xref-external-reg link previews the target
  through the new gated GET /api/provision/[id] (400 bad id, 401 signed out,
  403 no access, 404 via the visitor's own RLS-bound read) in the existing
  popup, with "Open in <regulation>" linking to
  /regulations/<reg>?from=<origin>#<id>. Modifier/middle clicks, links with
  no hash, and any failed fetch fall back to plain navigation.
- A reader opened with ?from=<provision of another regulation> shows
  "Back to <regulation> · <citation>" linking to the origin, and strips
  `from` from the URL (the entry's history state remembers it for reloads).
- Tests: reader-nav (jsdom, real component) and provision-preview (gate).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WUMyyKmSdfgERmWRQHrjdT
